# C# style rules for Homework Central backend

When editing C# files under `backend/`:

- Do not use `var`. Always write explicit types for locals, foreach variables, and deconstruction targets.
  This also covers pattern positions — write the real type in `is` and `case` patterns rather than
  `is var x` / `case var x`. The one unavoidable exception is an anonymous type assigned to a local,
  which has no nameable type; prefer keeping anonymous types inline so the exception does not arise.
- Do not use `dynamic` for locals or fields. `var` is statically typed and merely inferred, whereas
  `dynamic` defers binding to runtime.
- Enforced, not advisory: `csharp_style_var_*` is `error` in `.editorconfig` and
  `EnforceCodeStyleInBuild` is on, so an implicitly typed local fails `dotnet build` as `IDE0008`,
  and `scripts/check-no-var.sh` runs in CI for the cases the compiler cannot see. Do not suppress
  either — see `AGENTS.md` for the full rule.
- Prefer pattern matching (`switch` expressions, property/relational patterns) over large `if` / `else if` chains for closed-set decisions such as intake types, scan statuses, and account classes.
- Match existing naming, primary constructors, and file-scoped namespaces in the project.
- Before adding or changing comments, XML docs, Markdown, naming, or function structure, read and follow the Comment Documentation Guide at [`docs/COMMENT_DOCUMENTATION_GUIDE.md`](../../docs/COMMENT_DOCUMENTATION_GUIDE.md).
